NNAAMMEE
     aaxxggee — ASIX Electronics AX88178A/179/179A USB Gigabit Ethernet driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee xxhhccii
           ddeevviiccee eehhccii
           ddeevviiccee uuhhccii
           ddeevviiccee oohhccii
           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss
           ddeevviiccee uueetthheerr
           ddeevviiccee aaxxggee

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_axge_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaxxggee driver provides support for USB Gigabit Ethernet adapters based
     on the ASIX Electronics AX88179/AX88179A USB 3.0 and AX88178A USB 2.0
     chipsets.

     The AX88179, AX88179A and AX88178A contain a 10/100/1000 Ethernet MAC
     with a GMII interface for interfacing with the Gigabit Ethernet PHY.

     These devices will operate with both USB 1.x and USB 2.0 controllers, and
     the AX88179/AX88179A will operate with USB 3.0 controllers.  Packets are
     received and transmitted over separate USB bulk transfer endpoints.

     The aaxxggee driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                  user can manually override the autoselected mode by adding
                  media options to rc.conf(5).

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Set 10Mbps operation.  The ifconfig(8) mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can
                  also be used to select either ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx
                  modes.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX    Set 100Mbps (Fast Ethernet) operation.  The ifconfig(8)
                  mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can also be used to select either
                  ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes.

     11000000bbaasseeTT    Set 1000Mbps (Gigabit Ethernet) operation (AX88178 only).
                  The ifconfig(8) mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can also be used to select
                  either ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes.

     The aaxxggee driver supports the following media options:

     ffuullll--dduupplleexx  Force full duplex operation.

     hhaallff--dduupplleexx  Force half duplex operation.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

